Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_pixarlog.c
Line: 311
Function: horizontalAccumulate16
Bug type: out-of-bounds-write
CWE: CWE-787
Explanation: With stride == 0, the else-branch uses REPEAT(stride, ...) at line 311 which executes once due to the macro semantics (lines 109–118). n is not decreased and the subsequent while (n > 0) loop repeatedly increments/dereferences wp/op (lines 315–316), causing out-of-bounds memory access.

Source context:
```c
